      <title>How to replace a legacy tool with 100k installations</title>
      <subtitle>... and 50 reverse package dependencies in Debian</subtitle>
      <track>CrossDistribution Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Debian has a number of legacy tools (that&amp;#39;s a euphemism for ugly hacks) that are not addressed due to inertia, fear of breaking stuff, and the difficulty of reaching consensus for changes with cross-package impact. I&amp;#39;ll talk about dealing with the above issues in the context of ongoing work as part of Debian Enhancement Proposal 9.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Specifically, the talk will cover how (not) to make proposals for cross-package changes, and how to map behaviour in a technical spec to feature-centered assertions in a test suite.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
